            <div xml:id="d571">

                <pb facs="0566" n="556" xml:id="pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/10–649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-17T19:00:00-05:00">October 17, 1949—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>TelCan 728. Re Cantel 1167, Oct 6, request by Chief of Amer section FonOff for
                    info re US aid. Dept of opinion you shld not volunteer further reply. If FonOff
                    renews inquiry, however, you may say that Dept has informed you only that
                    interested agencies of US Govt now have under consideration the means by which
                    the policies and purposes declared in the Mutual Assistance Act can be
                    accomplished through expenditures in the general area of China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
